Z||000000||thecage||10-07-2001||11:37 PM||||Hello I need help. I just purchased an 86gt with 160,000kms. I have a hard time getting the car in third gear. sometimes it goes in smoothly sometimes I have to really struggle to get it to go in. Any suggestions would be helpful. Also what is the most effective way to lubricate the cables and with what product is best.<BR>thank you||||reg||1
Z||000001||Joe Torma||10-08-2001||12:49 AM||||Welcome!<P>Pop your decklid and get to the linkage on the trans.  Move to each gear using the levers and see if each one is easily selectable there.  You may have to adjust the cable on the select lever if you have no problem moving them.||||reg||1
Z||000002||SLYGUY||10-08-2001||01:26 AM||||Welcome... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Now check your fluid! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <P>No, seriously welcome to the Forum. <BR>It's a great place to find out more information about your new project...er... sports car.<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||TooManyFieros||10-08-2001||07:37 AM||||Sounds like a trans problem. If you checked your fluid, checked your cables and third is the only one giving you trouble, pull the trans apart and rebuild it. Sometimes, usind a better fluid like GM's "Syncromesh" will really help. I really noticed the difference (shifts real smooth now) and will never use anything else. Like Joe said, check the cables first and try new fliud. That is a good trans but sometimes, they just need some work. Also, used trans are available cheap.  TooManyFieros||||reg||1
Z||000004||thecage||10-08-2001||09:47 AM||||thanks everyone for information. i will have a look at both the fluid level and at the linkage at the transmission. i'm not mechanically inclined but am willing to learn. i'll let you know how it turns out.||||reg||1
Z||000005||thecage||10-08-2001||08:48 PM||||well i think the problem is solved. when i looked at the linkage the cable the provides the side movement had a piece of wire on it to hold it in place. i don't think it was necessary because i took the wire off and the rubber boot on the ball seemed to be a bit loose but not enough that it would have poped off. well i took it off and drove it for a while and the shifting seems to be better. do the gears need time to synronize or is it instant, cause the more i drove it the better the gears seemed to slip in place.<P>once again thank you everyone||||reg||1
